What Are Rubber Sheets?
Rubber sheets represent a fundamental industrial material - elastomers processed into uniform flat sheets with consistent thickness ranging from thin films to heavy 6mm+ gauges. Manufacturers typically supply these on rolls for easy handling and fabrication. When we examine their functionality, these sheets serve as the raw material for countless gaskets, seals, and protective components that prevent fluid/gas leakage in mechanical systems. What makes them particularly valuable is how material composition and thickness can be precisely matched to application requirements - whether that's chemical resistance in a processing plant or vibration dampening in automotive applications.
